WEBVTT

NOTE DATOM record page film. Generated by scripts/recordtour-captions.ts from recordtour/narration.json; do not hand edit.

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.090
AI cannot be fully trusted in science: it predicts a likely answer, and it does not check the evidence.

2
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:14.330
That is where verification comes in, and this is what it looks like: a DATOM record, read here from the top.

3
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:22.590
At the top is the claim in plain words, and under it the exact claim that was checked: who, at what dose, measured how, and for how long.

4
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.150
The record answers that question, and only that one.

5
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:31.650
51 studies tested it directly, and 44 say yes: 86%.

6
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.610
That count is where most summaries stop, and where this record starts.

7
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:41.710
Many of those studies share authors, labs and cohorts, so they are not 51 independent tests.

8
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.370
Weighted for how independent they really are, the evidence gives a range instead of a single number.

9
00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.070
The verdict bar shows that range, from 54.6% to 75.0%.

10
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:59.870
A claim is called Supported only when the bottom of its range clears 55%, and this one misses by four tenths of a point.

11
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:08.670
So the verdict is Contested, which does not mean refuted, and does not mean the studies are split: the evidence leans yes without settling it.

12
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:16.310
The evidence grade says how solid the evidence base is, and here it is B: solid, with a wide range.

13
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:21.750
A record is not medical advice: it checks one claim, not safety, dosing or side effects.

14
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:28.330
It says it was not commissioned or sponsored, and it dates every revision, keeping the earlier evaluation in its history.

15
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.870
The knowledge graph draws all 224 findings around the claim at the center.

16
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.810
Colour is each finding's relation to the claim, and a line is a relation a scan measured.

17
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.530
Drag to turn it, and select any mark to read that finding and its source.

18
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:48.770
Below it are the studies themselves, the three that weigh most first, each linked to the original paper.

19
00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:54.690
A record is a dated entry, not a live feed: it changes when DATOM examines the claim again.

20
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.630
Type a claim of your own, or paste a link.

21
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.930
The box is at the bottom of the page.

22
00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:01.950
DATOM.

23
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.890
Science, verified.

24
00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:04.900
For everyone.
